`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A dialogue runtime can persist its variables or interpreter state without persisting the world changes caused by its commands. Stopping dialogue can leave asynchronous game code running. An agent should therefore never translate “dialogue completed,” “variables saved,” or “story reset” directly into “quest transaction committed or rolled back.” Use the transaction template below to coordinate these states."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The newly examined Yarn Godot GDScript integration is ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Early Access 3.2"}),", requires the standard ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Godot 4.6+"})," build, and its README advises against shipping yet. The free source is separately available from paid add-ons. Installation docs and README disagree about whether the paid package is currently available, so no purchase or paid-feature availability claim is made. Sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://yarnspinner.dev/docs/godot/gdscript/01-installation/",children:"installation"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/README.md",children:"official repository"}),"."]}),`
