`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://yarnspinner.dev/docs/godot/gdscript/05-connecting-to-your-game/04-variables-and-storage/",children:"Variables and Storage, GDScript 3.2"})," documents ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"save_state_to_persistent_storage"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"load_state_from_persistent_storage"})," in ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"user://"}),"; both return booleans. Loading replaces current variables. Saved data excludes dialogue position: the application must retain a restart node and explicitly start it after loading. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"get_all_variables"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"set_all_variables"})," allow integration into an application save. A custom ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"YarnVariableStorage"})," can use the game's own data. Supported variable values are numbers, strings and booleans, not scene nodes or transforms. Subscriptions notify changes, not initial state; node-scoped subscriptions are removed when the node leaves the tree."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Pinned storage implementation:"})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/addons/yarn_spinner/dialogue_runner.gd#L1112-L1190",children:"runner save/load methods"})," serialize six parallel key/value arrays. Saving checks whether the file opened, then writes, closes and returns true without a post-write error check or readback; that return is not evidence of crash durability. Loading rejects non-dictionaries, absent/non-array sections and unequal key/value lengths before touching storage, but then converts keys and values to the declared types. It does not check a story hash or application schema. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/addons/yarn_spinner/core/in_memory_variable_storage.gd#L54-L158",children:"default storage"})," clears existing variables and repopulates them through individual setters; invalid names can be rejected without a failure result reaching the loader, and setters notify listeners during restoration. Thus a true load result is not proof of complete schema acceptance or an atomic observer-visible snapshot. Custom storage can differ. These are static source boundaries, not reproduced save failures."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate:"})," choose a restart-safe narrative boundary, retain the compiled program identity and restart node, and preserve the world-state save alongside variables. Rebuild UI/world presentation from the restored authoritative values instead of assuming a listener will replay every initial value. Missing or malformed saves, scene references and compatibility migration require project-specific handling; atomic writes, crash durability and runtime listener behavior during restore remain unverified."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"2-yarn-godot-stop-completion-is-not-command-cancellation",children:"2. Yarn Godot: stop completion is not command cancellation"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://yarnspinner.dev/docs/godot/gdscript/05-connecting-to-your-game/08-async-and-cancellation/",children:"Async and Cancellation, GDScript 3.2"})," distinguishes presenter hurry-up from next-content requests. Presenters must return before progression; a warning after five seconds is diagnostic rather than forced rollback. Commands have no presenter cancellation token. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"stop_dialogue()"})," can be awaited and emits ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dialogue_cancelled"})," followed by ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dialogue_completed"}),"; an already awaiting command can nevertheless keep executing its own code. The guide recommends checking running state after awaits. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"YarnAsync.wait"})," observes node processing/pause and ends when its node leaves the tree; a cancellation-token timeout keeps counting during pause."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Pinned lifecycle implementation:"})," the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/addons/yarn_spinner/dialogue_runner.gd#L1479-L1545",children:"runner"})," already captures ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"_run_id"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"_line_epoch"})," around awaited command handling and rejects stale completion before advancing current content. This protects the runner's continuation; it does not undo effects performed inside the command. The normal stop path waits for the completion promise, but ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/addons/yarn_spinner/dialogue_runner.gd#L250-L279",children:"tree-exit teardown"})," deliberately emits neither ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dialogue_cancelled"})," nor ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dialogue_completed"}),". A ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/addons/yarn_spinner/dialogue_runner.gd#L703-L717",children:"presenter-triggered restart during finishing"})," can also suppress the old run's completion signals. Therefore signal-only observers must not assume every ended run produces a pair of terminal events. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Godot-GDScript/blob/642e9ad61ff8e7dd01476fd5a89e675d380c3122/tests/test_dialogue_runner.gd#L113-L141",children:"upstream tests"})," cover ordinary stop signal counts and restart from a completion listener; they were read, not run, and do not establish external-effect cancellation."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate:"})," maintain application-owned conversation/session identity for external world commands as well as running state, complementing rather than replacing the runner's internal guards. A running-state check alone cannot prove an old command belongs to a newly started conversation. This is an editorial stale-world-effect hazard to test, not a claim that the runner lacks stale-continuation protection. After stopping, account for outstanding world commands independently before snapshotting, resetting or starting another scenario. Do not interpret a completed event as natural completion without recording cancellation intent and outcome."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"3-yarn-unreal-variable-slots-and-project-swaps-have-different-reset-scopes",children:"3. Yarn Unreal: variable slots and project swaps have different reset scopes"}),`
