`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["A native replay, a physics state vector and a narrative/database checkpoint restore different domains. Choose the baseline and reset mechanism before comparing agent edits. Preserve content/build identity, pending-work ownership, callback policy and the observation sequence; use independent state checks before interpreting a rendered frame as a successful reset. A source edit that changes replicated schemas, model topology or application effects may invalidate an old checkpoint even when a loader accepts it. The existing ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/production-debugging-contracts/#physics-recording-contact-and-restoration",children:"Jolt and CVD contracts"})," cover complementary physics recording and rollback limits; none of these mechanisms supplies universal game-state restoration. Actual round-trip fidelity, callback side effects and evaluation variance require a separately authorized disposable runtime fixture."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"stateful-interaction-discovery-and-failure-reduction",children:"Stateful interaction discovery and failure reduction"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Use stateful testing to discover and reduce action sequences that break an invariant. References below target the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/releases/tag/v6.170.1",children:"Hypothesis 6.170.1 release"})," and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/blob/718686d1e392968eb0953c043ef249c5d9d11a59/hypothesis/src/hypothesis/stateful.py",children:"state-machine implementation"})," at commit ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"718686d1e392968eb0953c043ef249c5d9d11a59"}),"; see the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/changelog.html",children:"changelog"})," for version changes."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"what-the-official-evidence-establishes",children:"What the official evidence establishes"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/stateful.html",children:"stateful guide"})," describes generating sequences of primitive actions and arguments, carrying earlier results through bundles, and comparing an implementation with a simpler reference model. Preconditions select applicable rules. By default, invariants wait until all initialization rules finish; check_during_init=True opts into initialization checks, and invariant preconditions can skip checks. Initialization precedes ordinary rules in an arbitrary order, but completion of every initializer is not guaranteed by a bounded trial; the source-level coverage qualification below applies. Its failure report is a short program, generally reusable as a regression test when argument representations are valid Python. This supports interaction-failure discovery, not exhaustive state coverage or game-quality assessment."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap application:"})," expose bounded actions such as press/release, advance fixed ticks, open/close menu, pause/resume, start/cancel dialogue, save/load and restart. Model only independently specified obligations: consumed keys are not reused, inventory is conserved under transfers, pause blocks the declared clock, and cancelled-session commands cannot modify a new session. A possible failing sequence is start dialogue → queue world command → cancel → restart → complete old command. Generation and shrinking could isolate the necessary order and arguments. This is an unimplemented fixture proposal, not evidence of a particular engine defect."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"a-completed-trial-need-not-have-exercised-gameplay",children:"A completed trial need not have exercised gameplay"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["In the pinned 6.170.1 implementation, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"stateful_step_count"})," limits the shared loop, including initialization. The stop decision occurs before selecting a pending initializer; after a selected initializer returns, it is not selected again. Default invariants are skipped while initializers remain, and teardown does not automatically check them again. ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Static control-flow example, not runtime reproduction:"})," a valid machine defining two non-failing initializers and at least one ordinary rule, with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"stateful_step_count=1"}),", only default invariants and default/no-op teardown, can finish a trial without executing an ordinary gameplay rule or any invariant. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/blob/718686d1e392968eb0953c043ef249c5d9d11a59/hypothesis/src/hypothesis/stateful.py#L140-L181",children:"Step selection and stopping, lines 140–181"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/blob/718686d1e392968eb0953c043ef249c5d9d11a59/hypothesis/src/hypothesis/stateful.py#L234-L238",children:"post-step checks and teardown, lines 234–238"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/blob/718686d1e392968eb0953c043ef249c5d9d11a59/hypothesis/src/hypothesis/stateful.py#L466-L480",children:"invariant skips, lines 466–480"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap gate:"})," record completed initializers, gameplay-rule executions and actual evaluations of each required assertion separately from the library's no-exception result. Declare minimum coverage for a completed acceptance trial; classify unmet coverage as unexercised/incomplete, not a gameplay pass. Do not discard genuine failures during initialization or shrinking because they lack later gameplay coverage. Do not enforce coverage with an unconditional teardown assertion that could replace the original failure. A future disposable fixture should define two initializers and an ordinary rule, then compare step ceilings of one, two and three, alongside an initialization failure and a skipped invariant. These are maximum lengths, not guaranteed counts; the loop can stop early. Preserve observed counts and cleanup outcomes. This fixture remains unimplemented and unexecuted."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"a-new-machine-does-not-reset-the-game",children:"A new machine does not reset the game"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_modules/hypothesis/stateful.html",children:"rendered stateful implementation"})," calls the machine factory inside each generated test case, then runs rules/invariants under a ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"try/finally"})," that calls teardown. Default teardown does nothing. Factory construction precedes that protected region, so partial construction needs its own cleanup. The generated TestCase defaults to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"deadline=None"})," and suppressed health checks. These are static source observations, not measured behavior in an installed release."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed gate:"})," every candidate, including shrink attempts, must establish the same declared starting state. Record whether isolation means fresh process, scene reload or checkpoint restoration. Explicitly reset held input, save directory, singleton/session state, pending jobs, RNG streams and relevant services; do not assume a new Python object performs these operations. Separate reset/boot failures from gameplay failures. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/api.html#hypothesis.HealthCheck.function_scoped_fixture",children:"API reference"})," warns that function-scoped pytest fixtures reset per test function, not per generated input; required per-input isolation must be implemented explicitly."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"reduction-fresh-replay-and-flakiness",children:"Reduction, fresh replay and flakiness"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorial/flaky.html",children:"flakiness guide"})," requires stable outcomes and stable Hypothesis-visible generation calls for repeated inputs. Unreset filesystem/database/global state, unmanaged randomness, scheduling and network timing can invalidate that assumption. A failure that disappears on replay raises ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"FlakyFailure"}),"; unstable strategies can prevent reliable reduction."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed evidence contract:"})," retain the initial trace, reduced trace, failed invariant, action arguments, tick boundaries and reset identity. Preserve each trace separately from its execution attempts. Then replay the reduced trace from independently established clean state before promoting it into the fixed regression suite. Shrink evaluations are adaptive search work, not independent success-rate trials. Label a trace “reduced by the configured search”; do not imply a proof of globally shortest causation. If the failure disappears, retain the discrepancy as flaky/unresolved rather than silently accepting a pass."]}),`
